<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>West Virginia Drops First Game to No. 13 Notre Dame</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-basketball-west-virginia-drops-first-game-to-no-13-notre-dame</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-basketball-west-virginia-drops-first-game-to-no-13-notre-dame</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WBB Team during the Battle 4 Atlantis game against Notre Dame" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG" /><br /><br />PARADISE ISLAND, Bahamas – West Virginia battled back from a slow start and cut a 17-point halftime deficit to eight in the third quarter, but Notre Dame pulled away late for a 78-64 victory on Thursday at Atlantis Resort. The loss dropped WVU to 6-1 on the season.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG"><media:title>WBB Team during the Battle 4 Atlantis game against Notre Dame</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:12:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59766</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Host Texas Tech for Senior Day in Regular Season Finale</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/volleyball-mountaineers-host-texas-tech-for-senior-day-in-regular-season-finale</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/volleyball-mountaineers-host-texas-tech-for-senior-day-in-regular-season-finale</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Alexis Finnvold and Mirjam Kask high five after a point in the match against Baylor" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-14, 6-11 Big 12) closes out the 2026 regular season on Friday, Nov. 27, welcoming Texas Tech to Hope Coliseum for Senior Day. First serve is set for 3 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg"><media:title>Alexis Finnvold and Mirjam Kask high five after a point in the match against Baylor</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:52:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59765</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Virginia-North Carolina to Meet in Charlotte on Friday Night</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/mens-basketball-west-virginia-north-carolina-to-meet-in-charlotte-on-friday-night</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/mens-basketball-west-virginia-north-carolina-to-meet-in-charlotte-on-friday-night</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia guard Miles Sadler celebrates a basket during the Mountaineers' season-opening victory over Niagara at Hope Coliseum on Monday, Nov. 2, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia meets North Carolina on Friday, Nov. 27, at the Spectrum Center in Charlotte, North Carolina, in the second annual Dick Vitale Invitational being put on by ESPN Events and the Charlotte Sports Foundation.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia guard Miles Sadler celebrates a basket during the Mountaineers' season-opening victory over Niagara at Hope Coliseum on Monday, Nov. 2, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:52:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59754</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Head to Charlottesville for Second Round of NCAA Tournament</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-soccer-mountaineers-head-to-charlottesville-for-second-round-of-ncaa-tournament</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-soccer-mountaineers-head-to-charlottesville-for-second-round-of-ncaa-tournament</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Layla Thompson dribbles a ball during a match." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg" /><br /><br />CHARLOTTESVILLE, Va. – The No. 7-seed West Virginia University women's soccer team continues its 25th NCAA Tournament appearance when it travels to No. 2-seed Virginia for the Second Round on Friday, Nov. 20. Kickoff at Kl&ouml;ckner Stadium in Charlottesville, Virginia, is slated for 6 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg"><media:title>Layla Thompson dribbles a ball during a match.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:14:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59764</s:story_id></item><item><title>So Long Milan Puskar Stadium Press Box: Demolition of the 46-Year-Old Structure Underway</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/so-long-milan-puskar-stadium-press-box-demolition-of-the-46-year-old-structure-underway</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/so-long-milan-puskar-stadium-press-box-demolition-of-the-46-year-old-structure-underway</guid><category>Football, General</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="A recent view of the Milan Puskar Stadium press box, which served the stadium from 1980 to 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/24/press_box__8-23-08_by_TG_.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Milan Puskar Stadium's hulking, 46-year-old press box is meeting the wrecking ball to make way for a new $150 million West Tower scheduled to be completed before the start of the 2028 football season.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/press_box__8-23-08_by_TG_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/press_box__8-23-08_by_TG_.jpg"><media:title>A recent view of the Milan Puskar Stadium press box, which served the stadium from 1980 to 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/press_box__8-23-08_by_TG_.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>3</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59762</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Fall to No. 20 Baylor in Three Sets</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/25/volleyball-mountaineers-fall-to-no-20-baylor-in-three-sets</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/25/volleyball-mountaineers-fall-to-no-20-baylor-in-three-sets</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball team huddles during the match against Baylor" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/25/Volleyball_vBaylor_112526-4.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-14, 6-11 Big 12) fell to No. 20 Baylor in straight sets on Wednesday afternoon at Hope Coliseum. The Mountaineers dropped the match by set scores of 25-22, 25-19 and 26-24.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/Volleyball_vBaylor_112526-4.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/Volleyball_vBaylor_112526-4.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball team huddles during the match against Baylor</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/Volleyball_vBaylor_112526-4.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:35:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59763</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers to Meet Second-Ranked Utah Friday Night in Salt Lake City</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/25/football-mountaineers-to-meet-second-ranked-utah-friday-night-in-salt-lake-city</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/25/football-mountaineers-to-meet-second-ranked-utah-friday-night-in-salt-lake-city</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Head coach Rich Rodriguez walks the sidelines against Cincinnati  at Milan Puskar Stadium on Oct. 17, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/17/32_GAMEACTION_WVU_UC_GM7.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The Great Talent Redistribution going on in college football right now as a result of Name, Image and Likeness (NIL) and direct revenue sharing is requiring a reexamination of things.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/32_GAMEACTION_WVU_UC_GM7.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/32_GAMEACTION_WVU_UC_GM7.jpg"><media:title>Head coach Rich Rodriguez walks the sidelines against Cincinnati  at Milan Puskar Stadium on Oct. 17, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/32_GAMEACTION_WVU_UC_GM7.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:47:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59760</s:story_id></item><item><title>Legendary Broadcaster Jay Jacobs Passes Away at Age 88</title><link>https://wvusports.co